From fba8f6a564d20c00742f83b620abc785cf96ded3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:38:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iop: module unload frees its memory; reset failures are
 reported; stack arguments are validated; SIF handshake (H-IOP9, H-IOP11,
 H-IOP12, H-IOP14, review-51 SIF)

H-IOP9: stopModule and a NO_RESIDENT_END start never returned the image block or
the module metadata, so load/unload cycles exhausted the 2 MiB pool (-400).
- stopModule now revokes everything that points into the image (threads - also
  by entry point -, alarms, RPC servers and exports as before, plus interrupt
  and timer handlers, ioman devices, CDVD callbacks, queued completion events
  and the SECR/MODLOAD hooks) and then frees the image and metadata
- a non-resident start frees its backing when no callback still points into
  it; a module that deliberately leaves a handler/device/callback behind
  keeps its backing until reset exactly as before
- a load that is rejected before its start routine runs, including every
  failure inside the image loader after the block was reserved, returns the
  block; the dead moduleCursor is removed

H-IOP11: IopSubsystem::reset() ignored tryReset() failure, and the ELF loader
used it, so old modules, RPC servers and the SPU could survive into the next
program unnoticed. reset() now throws like PS2Runtime::resetIop(), the ELF
load fails with a message, and IopRpcBridge::reset() no longer silently skips
its reset when the retirement observer cannot be reinstalled.

H-IOP12: SifSendCmd and SifRegisterRpc read their o32 stack arguments with
read32, which yields 0 for memory the IOP does not own, so a bad frame
registered null callbacks. Both now validate the frame (readStackArguments).

H-IOP14 / review-51 F1-F2: the HLE sceSifInitCmd now raises SMFLAG 0x20000
between sceSifInit's 0x10000 and the boot-end 0x40000, as the SDK handshake
does (the EE observed 0x50000 only); a test pins that order and the
register-number mapping handed to the host. Kprintf formats its arguments
(shared printf formatter) instead of logging the raw format string. The
no-op onSifTransfer in the emulator and bridge, Impl::lastError and the
mutable activity counter are removed, the ioman test friend is test-only.

Tests: module lifecycle (leak check verified by mutation), reset reporting,
stack-argument validation, SIF handshake/numbering, Kprintf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
